{"id":"a7eff3413ce92299","group":"58","path":"58/batch08/58-df-transition-matrix.md","title":"Transition Matrix","display":"df-transition-matrix — Transition Matrix","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-transition-matrix","aliases":["58-df-transition-matrix","Transition Matrix"],"display":"df-transition-matrix — Transition Matrix","depends_on":["[[../batch07/58-df-probability-space.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-transition-matrix"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-transition-matrix</span><span>Transition Matrix</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-transition-matrix — Transition Matrix"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"0578a357a86e9d8f\" href=\"?note=0578a357a86e9d8f\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-probability-space.md\">../batch07/58-df-probability-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P,S,X,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P\\in V\">\\(P,S,X,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"0578a357a86e9d8f\" href=\"?note=0578a357a86e9d8f\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-probability-space.md\">../batch07/58-df-probability-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S\\subseteq V^6\">\\(\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S\\subseteq V^6\\)</span> (transition-matrix predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}transition\\text{-}matrix}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S(P,X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\n\\land S\\neq\\varnothing\\land|S|\\leq\\aleph_0\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(X,\\omega\\times\\Omega,S)\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(P,S\\times S,[0,1])\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall i\\in S\\;\\left(\\sum_{j\\in S}P(\\langle i,j\\rangle)=1\\right)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall i,j\\in S\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathbb P(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:X(\\langle n,\\xi\\rangle)=i\\})&gt;0\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{10em}\\to\nP(\\langle i,j\\rangle)\\,\\mathbb P(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:X(\\langle n,\\xi\\rangle)=i\\})\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{13em}=\n\\mathbb P(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:X(\\langle n,\\xi\\rangle)=i\n\\land X(\\langle n+1,\\xi\\rangle)=j\\})\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}transition\\text{-}matrix}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S(P,X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\n\\land S\\neq\\varnothing\\land|S|\\leq\\aleph_0\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(X,\\omega\\times\\Omega,S)\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(P,S\\times S,[0,1])\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall i\\in S\\;\\left(\\sum_{j\\in S}P(\\langle i,j\\rangle)=1\\right)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall i,j\\in S\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathbb P(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:X(\\langle n,\\xi\\rangle)=i\\})&gt;0\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{10em}\\to\nP(\\langle i,j\\rangle)\\,\\mathbb P(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:X(\\langle n,\\xi\\rangle)=i\\})\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{13em}=\n\\mathbb P(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:X(\\langle n,\\xi\\rangle)=i\n\\land X(\\langle n+1,\\xi\\rangle)=j\\})\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The event arguments of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb P\">\\(\\mathbb P\\)</span> are actual subsets of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega\">\\(\\Omega\\)</span>, not truth values.</li>\n<li>This predicate records time-homogeneous one-step conditional probabilities. The Markov property relative to the entire past is a separate condition.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P^n\">\\(P^n\\)</span>: entries give <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>-step transition probabilities</li>\n<li>Stationary: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi P = \\pi\">\\(\\pi P = \\pi\\)</span> (left eigenvector with eigenvalue 1)</li>\n<li>Spectral: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda_1 = 1\">\\(\\lambda_1 = 1\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|\\lambda_i| \\leq 1\">\\(|\\lambda_i| \\leq 1\\)</span> for all <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"i\">\\(i\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Norris, Markov Chains</li>\n<li>Meyn and Tweedie, Markov Chains and Stochastic Stability</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch07/58-df-probability-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"0578a357a86e9d8f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-probability-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-probability-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"0578a357a86e9d8f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}\\subseteq V^3$ (see [[../batch07/58-df-probability-space.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^3$ (see [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"P,S,X,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}\\subseteq V^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S\\subseteq V^6","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}transition\\text{-}matrix}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S(P,X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\\\\n&\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\n\\land S\\neq\\varnothing\\land|S|\\leq\\aleph_0\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(X,\\omega\\times\\Omega,S)\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(P,S\\times S,[0,1])\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land\\forall i\\in S\\;\\left(\\sum_{j\\in S}P(\\langle i,j\\rangle)=1\\right)\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall i,j\\in S\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathbb P(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:X(\\langle n,\\xi\\rangle)=i\\})>0\\\\\n&\\hspace{10em}\\to\nP(\\langle i,j\\rangle)\\,\\mathbb P(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:X(\\langle n,\\xi\\rangle)=i\\})\\\\\n&\\hspace{13em}=\n\\mathbb P(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:X(\\langle n,\\xi\\rangle)=i\n\\land X(\\langle n+1,\\xi\\rangle)=j\\})\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathbb P","display":false},{"tex":"\\Omega","display":false},{"tex":"P^n","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi P = \\pi","display":false},{"tex":"\\lambda_1 = 1","display":false},{"tex":"|\\lambda_i| \\leq 1","display":false},{"tex":"i","display":false}],"bytes":2052,"backlinks":[{"id":"c050de49950a0f5f","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"a7d38e47660167fe","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S(P,X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)$ (transition-matrix predicate, see [[../batch08/58-df-transition-matrix.md]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1314","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-transition-matrix.md|58-df-transition-matrix]]（batch08）"}],"outgoing":["0578a357a86e9d8f","36d7463d215be751"]}